<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE components PUBLIC "-//DBFLUTE//DTD LastaDi 1.0//EN"
	"http://dbflute.org/meta/lastadi10.dtd">
<components>
	<!-- SsoAuthenticator components are provided by fess-sso-* plugins via fess_sso++.xml.
	     SsoManager resolves them as "<sso.type>Authenticator", and the ++ suffix merges into this
	     file, so it stays even though core registers nothing but the manager: without a base file
	     the plugins have nowhere to contribute to.

	     Keeping the sso.type-to-class mapping in the DI definition rather than in Java is what
	     makes that work. Setting sso.type to a component's name is enough to reach it, so a plugin
	     needs no change here to be reachable. An sso.type whose plugin is not installed is a
	     configuration error SsoManager reports rather than a missing class.

	     Do not add a fess_sso++.xml here for a component a plugin also registers: two definitions
	     of one name make getComponent throw TooManyRegistrationComponentException, and the
	     postConstruct that registers the authenticator with this manager runs twice. There is no
	     way to override one from the other either, because a redefinition file has to be named
	     fess_sso+&lt;component&gt;.xml and a base path containing a plus sign is exactly what
	     RedefinableComponentTagHandler.redefine() refuses. -->
	<component name="ssoManager" class="org.codelibs.fess.sso.SsoManager">
	</component>
</components>
